== 6.9 Chapter 6 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Water and mineral salts are transported in a plant by the],
  [cortex],
  [phloem],
  [xylem],
  [pith]
)

#mcq(2, [The process by which water moves from the soil into a root hair cell is],
  [active transport],
  [diffusion],
  [osmosis],
  [translocation]
)

#mcq(3, [Transpiration is faster when the air is],
  [cold and dry],
  [dry and windy],
  [warm and humid],
  [humid and still]
)

#mcq(4, [Mineral salts enter a root hair cell by active transport because],
  [they are dissolved in water],
  [their concentration is higher inside the cell],
  [the cell has no nucleus],
  [osmosis carries them]
)

#mcq(5, [The loss of water vapour from the leaves of a plant is called],
  [translocation],
  [transpiration],
  [respiration],
  [guttation]
)

#mcq(6, [Sugar is transported in a plant by the],
  [phloem],
  [cambium],
  [epidermis],
  [xylem]
)

#mcq(7, [Which of these would *increase* the rate of transpiration?],
  [Increasing wind speed],
  [Removing the leaves],
  [Increasing humidity],
  [Closing the stomata]
)

#mcq(8, [A root hair cell has many mitochondria because],
  [it stores starch],
  [it needs energy for active transport],
  [it divides rapidly],
  [it photosynthesises]
)

#mcq(9, [The transpiration pull is the force that],
  [closes the stomata],
  [draws water up the xylem],
  [pushes water down the phloem],
  [opens the stomata]
)

#mcq(10, [Which statement about the phloem is correct?],
  [It is made of dead cells],
  [It has lignified walls],
  [It consists of living cells with sieve plates],
  [It carries only water]
)

#mcq(11, [The cuticle of a leaf reduces transpiration because it is],
  [transparent],
  [porous],
  [green],
  [waxy and waterproof]
)

#mcq(12, [Water travels from cell to cell across the root by],
  [translocation],
  [diffusion of water vapour],
  [osmosis],
  [active transport of water]
)

#mcq(13, [In a potometer, the shoot is cut under water in order to],
  [prevent air from entering the xylem],
  [remove the leaves],
  [keep it cool],
  [increase the rate of uptake]
)

#mcq(14, [Which of the following is a xerophytic adaptation?],
  [Large, thin leaves],
  [Sunken stomata and a thick cuticle],
  [Many stomata on the upper surface],
  [Aerial roots]
)

#mcq(15, [Wilting of a plant is caused by],
  [loss of turgor pressure],
  [excess water uptake],
  [damage to the phloem],
  [a rise in chlorophyll]
)

#mcq(16, [The movement of sugars through the phloem is called],
  [transpiration],
  [osmosis],
  [diffusion],
  [translocation]
)

#mcq(17, [Guttation is the loss of water from a plant as],
  [ice on the leaf],
  [water in the phloem],
  [liquid droplets through hydathodes],
  [vapour through the stomata]
)

#mcq(18, [Which process does *not* require energy from respiration?],
  [Uptake of potassium ions],
  [Loading sucrose into the phloem],
  [Osmosis of water into a root hair],
  [Active transport of nitrate ions]
)

#mcq(19, [A plant ring-barked with the bark removed will eventually die because],
  [the leaves stop photosynthesising],
  [the xylem is destroyed],
  [the phloem is destroyed and sugar cannot reach the roots],
  [water cannot enter the roots]
)

#mcq(20, [The main force that moves water up a tall tree is],
  [capillary action alone],
  [transpiration pull],
  [root pressure alone],
  [active transport in the xylem]
)

#mcq(21, [Which of these tissues consists of dead cells at maturity?],
  [Palisade mesophyll],
  [Xylem],
  [Cambium],
  [Phloem]
)

#mcq(22, [Water potential is highest in],
  [pure water],
  [the cell sap of the root hair],
  [dry soil],
  [a concentrated sugar solution]
)

#mcq(23, [The stomata of most leaves are found],
  [mainly on the lower surface],
  [only on the upper surface],
  [in the veins],
  [on the cuticle]
)

#mcq(24, [Guard cells open the stoma when they],
  [lose their chloroplasts],
  [die],
  [lose water and become flaccid],
  [take up water and become turgid]
)

#mcq(25, [Which of these is *not* a function of transpiration?],
  [Making glucose],
  [Carrying mineral salts upwards],
  [Cooling the leaf],
  [Drawing water up the xylem]
)

#mcq(26, [The ascent of water in the xylem is helped by cohesion, which means],
  [water molecules repel each other],
  [water molecules stick to one another],
  [xylem contains air],
  [water molecules stick to the walls]
)

#mcq(27, [An experiment shows a plant loses water faster in a windy place. This is because wind],
  [raises the humidity around the leaf],
  [closes the stomata],
  [increases chlorophyll],
  [removes the humid layer around the leaf]
)

#mcq(28, [Which of these would reduce water loss from a leaf?],
  [Removing the cuticle],
  [Opening the stomata wider],
  [Increasing the leaf area],
  [Rolling the leaf]
)

#mcq(29, [Root hairs are adapted for absorption because they],
  [contain chloroplasts],
  [are covered with a thick cuticle],
  [store starch],
  [greatly increase the absorbing surface]
)

#mcq(30, [A plant wilts on a hot day but recovers at night because],
  [the roots grow],
  [respiration stops],
  [photosynthesis stops],
  [transpiration falls at night while absorption continues]
)

